1
00:00:27,527 --> 00:00:30,948
THE HUSBAND

2
00:00:35,202 --> 00:00:36,410
THIS SERIES IS FICTITIOUS

3
00:00:36,411 --> 00:00:39,039
CHILDREN WERE FILMED SAFELY
GEN AI WAS USED IN SELECT SCENES

4
00:00:39,998 --> 00:00:40,999
To pick up the money.

5
00:00:41,708 --> 00:00:43,125
What? Money?

6
00:00:43,126 --> 00:00:44,711
The three billion you have here.

7
00:00:45,337 --> 00:00:48,548
I need you to hand it over to me.

8
00:00:48,549 --> 00:00:51,385
Let Seyun go first.
Then I'll give you the money.

9
00:00:52,052 --> 00:00:53,135
No, Mother.

10
00:00:53,136 --> 00:00:56,097
Give me the money first.
That's the only way she'll live.

11
00:00:56,098 --> 00:00:57,723
What?

12
00:00:57,724 --> 00:00:59,101
You greedy bastard.

13
00:01:20,998 --> 00:01:22,332
Here's your money as promised.

14
00:01:23,667 --> 00:01:24,668
For real this time.

15
00:01:25,502 --> 00:01:27,462
You've gotten pretty smart, Mr. Kang.

16
00:01:29,214 --> 00:01:30,465
All right, Mr. Kang.

17
00:01:31,258 --> 00:01:33,134
Why don't we talk this out?

18
00:01:33,135 --> 00:01:36,721
At 8 p.m. tonight,
wait in front of Dong Nam Sports Center.

19
00:01:36,722 --> 00:01:39,600
I'll tell you the exact location then.

20
00:01:45,814 --> 00:01:46,982
Where do I meet you?

21
00:01:49,818 --> 00:01:50,861
Mr. Kang.

22
00:01:51,778 --> 00:01:53,488
Come to Do San Development Company.

23
00:01:54,197 --> 00:01:55,407
You have 10 minutes.

24
00:02:14,468 --> 00:02:15,552
Is this the police?

25
00:02:17,220 --> 00:02:19,096
EPISODE 9

26
00:02:19,097 --> 00:02:22,100
EMERGENCY SERVICES, AMBULANCE

27
00:02:46,375 --> 00:02:47,750
-  Hey, Choi.
- Yes, sir.

28
00:02:47,751 --> 00:02:48,752
This way.

29
00:02:59,596 --> 00:03:00,763
Critical?

30
00:03:00,764 --> 00:03:03,766
These people are criminals
that did horrible things to my daughter.

31
00:03:03,767 --> 00:03:05,435
How could I let them in my hospital?

32
00:03:07,229 --> 00:03:08,480
You, say something.

33
00:03:09,064 --> 00:03:10,898
Have you forgotten what you've done?

34
00:03:10,899 --> 00:03:14,735
You orchestrated the hit on my daughter,

35
00:03:14,736 --> 00:03:18,323
you broke into my home with a gun
and took three billion won from me.

36
00:03:19,074 --> 00:03:21,575
You really think you have
any right to be in this room?

37
00:03:21,576 --> 00:03:24,121
Well, I took the money for a reason.

38
00:03:24,788 --> 00:03:26,664
I couldn't tell you at the time.

39
00:03:26,665 --> 00:03:30,001
I was planning to give it back
as soon as I got Seyun back.

40
00:03:30,836 --> 00:03:34,214
Then where's my three billion?

41
00:03:35,257 --> 00:03:36,258
Let me see it now!

42
00:03:37,259 --> 00:03:38,885
I put it in my trunk.

43
00:03:39,719 --> 00:03:41,053
What?

44
00:03:41,054 --> 00:03:44,599
I put it in the trunk
of the car I was driving.

45
00:03:45,684 --> 00:03:47,310
-  Check the trunk.
- Yes, sir.

46
00:03:48,145 --> 00:03:51,106
Honestly,
I still don't know what to believe.

47
00:03:51,690 --> 00:03:54,526
Whether you were actually
trying to save your wife,

48
00:03:55,193 --> 00:03:58,113
or you just ended up saving her
when things went sideways.

49
00:03:58,822 --> 00:04:01,449
Let's say you're telling the truth.

50
00:04:01,450 --> 00:04:04,286
But what about the money?
Where is that three billion?

51
00:04:04,870 --> 00:04:07,872
I told you. I left it in the trunk.

52
00:04:07,873 --> 00:04:10,083
We searched the whole thing
but found nothing.

53
00:04:11,126 --> 00:04:13,377
So be honest with us, Mr. Kang.

54
00:04:13,378 --> 00:04:17,507
If what you said were true,
the money would've been in the trunk.

55
00:04:19,718 --> 00:04:22,511
We don't know what else we'll find,
so search every inch.

56
00:04:22,512 --> 00:04:23,513
Yes, sir.

57
00:04:27,058 --> 00:04:28,184
What's that?

58
00:04:28,185 --> 00:04:30,437
It's a cell phone.
It was under the fridge.

59
00:04:31,271 --> 00:04:32,563
-  The fridge?
- Yeah.

60
00:04:32,564 --> 00:04:33,690
Captain.

61
00:04:34,858 --> 00:04:36,150
You should see this.

62
00:04:36,151 --> 00:04:38,861
COME TO THE HOSPITAL
WE NEED TO TALK

63
00:04:38,862 --> 00:04:39,905
"To the hospital"?

64
00:04:40,489 --> 00:04:43,366
- Is that all?
- Yeah, everything else was wiped clean.

65
00:04:44,826 --> 00:04:47,871
Get Kim Gyeongae's phone
to Forensics now.

66
00:04:48,455 --> 00:04:50,373
And track down the owner of this number.

67
00:04:51,833 --> 00:04:53,292
What?

68
00:04:53,293 --> 00:04:55,337
Kang Taeju was there?

69
00:04:56,129 --> 00:04:57,589
Why are you telling me this now?

70
00:04:58,340 --> 00:05:01,384
I'll take care of it myself.
Just come to the hospital.

71
00:05:04,971 --> 00:05:08,015
Darn, Kang Taeju.
If only he hadn't shown up.

72
00:05:10,185 --> 00:05:12,979
INCOMING CALL

73
00:05:46,471 --> 00:05:49,224
PROCEED AS PLANNED

74
00:05:59,067 --> 00:06:00,068
MESSAGES
NEW MESSAGE

75
00:06:20,589 --> 00:06:21,590
Honey.

76
00:06:23,133 --> 00:06:24,633
Hang in there.

77
00:06:24,634 --> 00:06:29,556
THE HUSBAND

78
00:06:34,269 --> 00:06:38,023
FORENSICS
POLICE

79
00:06:39,357 --> 00:06:40,400
POTASSIUM CHLORIDE

80
00:07:07,093 --> 00:07:09,678
NEUROSURGERY
HA JEONGSOO

81
00:07:09,679 --> 00:07:12,181
DO NOT CROSS, POLICE LINE
UNDER INVESTIGATION

82
00:07:20,482 --> 00:07:23,902
You came down here, looking for
Ha Jeongsoo and called his phone,

83
00:07:24,611 --> 00:07:26,905
you heard his phone ringing
by the emergency stairs,

84
00:07:27,405 --> 00:07:30,157
and found him collapsed there.

85
00:07:30,158 --> 00:07:31,241
Is that correct?

86
00:07:31,242 --> 00:07:32,494
Yeah, that's correct.

87
00:07:33,912 --> 00:07:36,246
But why were you
looking for him anyway?

88
00:07:41,169 --> 00:07:43,213
What… Is it true?

89
00:07:43,755 --> 00:07:45,340
Dr. Ha is dead?

90
00:07:46,424 --> 00:07:47,425
Yes.

91
00:07:49,719 --> 00:07:51,345
I need to see him myself.

92
00:07:51,346 --> 00:07:53,931
Forensics is in there right now.

93
00:07:53,932 --> 00:07:55,225
You're not allowed.

94
00:07:59,688 --> 00:08:00,689
Are you okay?

95
00:08:01,648 --> 00:08:02,649
Yeah.

96
00:08:03,149 --> 00:08:04,733
How did Dr. Ha end up…

97
00:08:04,734 --> 00:08:07,028
What in the world happened?

98
00:08:08,571 --> 00:08:10,989
We're looking into that right now.

99
00:08:10,990 --> 00:08:15,911
Director Ko should be able to tell you
a lot more about Dr. Ha than I can.

100
00:08:23,753 --> 00:08:26,297
He was going to meet Dr. Ha last night.

101
00:08:28,925 --> 00:08:30,009
Is that correct?

102
00:08:30,760 --> 00:08:32,345
I… Well…

103
00:08:33,263 --> 00:08:37,058
He called out of the blue last night
about an emergency,

104
00:08:38,101 --> 00:08:40,895
so I came to the hospital like he asked.

105
00:08:42,355 --> 00:08:45,525
But when I arrived, I couldn't find him.

106
00:08:46,234 --> 00:08:47,694
I couldn't reach him either,

107
00:08:48,737 --> 00:08:49,987
so…

108
00:08:49,988 --> 00:08:53,408
I went back home after a while.

109
00:08:55,285 --> 00:08:56,286
What?

110
00:08:57,454 --> 00:08:59,122
What are you saying?

111
00:08:59,622 --> 00:09:01,790
Calm down.

112
00:09:01,791 --> 00:09:03,542
I can't understand a word!

113
00:09:05,628 --> 00:09:08,298
You know what a huge problem
you've caused?

114
00:09:08,965 --> 00:09:10,591
Where are you right now?

115
00:09:10,592 --> 00:09:14,053
No. Just come back to the hospital!

116
00:09:18,349 --> 00:09:21,352
Detective Oh. Yeah, got it.

117
00:09:22,812 --> 00:09:24,938
I'm going to check
the surveillance footage.

118
00:09:24,939 --> 00:09:26,190
Give me a minute.

119
00:09:26,191 --> 00:09:28,276
I'll go with you.

120
00:09:29,569 --> 00:09:30,695
Be right back.

121
00:09:49,506 --> 00:09:52,091
This is the parking garage last night.

122
00:09:52,092 --> 00:09:56,805
SECTOR A

123
00:09:58,056 --> 00:10:00,350
And this is after Mr. Ha walked past.

124
00:10:01,684 --> 00:10:03,728
First comes Director Ko.

125
00:10:05,730 --> 00:10:06,981
This is the parking area.

126
00:10:14,322 --> 00:10:15,824
Next comes Mr. Kang.

127
00:10:20,954 --> 00:10:23,373
- Yeah, it's just like Mr. Kang said.
- Right.

128
00:10:26,459 --> 00:10:30,212
And this is Mr. Ha taking the elevator
up to the hospital.

129
00:10:30,213 --> 00:10:34,175
MAIN BUILDING E/V #3

130
00:10:45,145 --> 00:10:46,229
Hold on.

131
00:10:46,813 --> 00:10:48,313
Did he go right back down?

132
00:10:48,314 --> 00:10:49,315
Yeah.

133
00:10:50,024 --> 00:10:52,986
Who was that on the elevator with him?

134
00:10:57,699 --> 00:10:59,117
Dr. Cha Myeonghui.

135
00:11:01,953 --> 00:11:04,873
To be honest,
I was a bit stunned when I got the call.

136
00:11:06,833 --> 00:11:10,461
I had no idea that Dr. Ha
would do anything like that.

137
00:11:11,045 --> 00:11:16,593
So, you were on the elevator
with him last night, correct?

138
00:11:17,886 --> 00:11:18,969
Yes.

139
00:11:18,970 --> 00:11:22,891
Would you mind telling us
what you guys talked about?

140
00:11:23,600 --> 00:11:26,936
I said hi to him,
but he didn't say anything.

141
00:11:27,854 --> 00:11:31,648
He didn't look so well,
so I asked if he was okay.

142
00:11:31,649 --> 00:11:32,942
So, what did he say?

143
00:11:33,568 --> 00:11:35,403
He just said he was fine.

144
00:11:36,863 --> 00:11:39,616
But something was off about him.

145
00:11:40,408 --> 00:11:44,077
It sounded like he was
talking to himself under his breath.

146
00:11:44,078 --> 00:11:45,371
Talking to himself?

147
00:11:46,331 --> 00:11:47,707
Do you know what he was saying?

148
00:11:48,625 --> 00:11:50,083
Uh…

149
00:11:50,084 --> 00:11:52,503
I didn't quite make out
what he was saying.

150
00:11:53,171 --> 00:11:55,715
I just told him to come to me
if he's struggling.

151
00:11:56,507 --> 00:11:59,344
That's all I could do for him.

152
00:12:00,261 --> 00:12:03,348
I had no idea that would be the last time.

153
00:12:04,015 --> 00:12:07,809
Well, do you happen to know
why he took the same elevator down

154
00:12:07,810 --> 00:12:08,937
to the basement?

155
00:12:10,647 --> 00:12:13,899
No, I got off before that,
so I don't know.

156
00:12:13,900 --> 00:12:16,361
Right. Of course.

157
00:12:17,070 --> 00:12:21,032
So what was he like on an average day?

158
00:12:21,616 --> 00:12:22,700
Anything peculiar?

159
00:12:23,409 --> 00:12:28,121
It's hard to say for sure
since we never had a formal consultation.

160
00:12:28,122 --> 00:12:30,291
But the past few times
I ran into him recently,

161
00:12:31,292 --> 00:12:33,253
he did seem a bit on edge.

162
00:12:34,254 --> 00:12:36,046
I wouldn't say he was anxious,

163
00:12:36,047 --> 00:12:39,384
but like he had a lot
weighing on his mind.

164
00:12:42,637 --> 00:12:43,638
All right.

165
00:12:44,222 --> 00:12:46,765
And thank you for your time.

166
00:12:46,766 --> 00:12:49,726
I'll let you know if I remember
anything that might help.

167
00:12:49,727 --> 00:12:50,979
You can call me anytime.

168
00:12:51,604 --> 00:12:53,523
Yeah, we appreciate it.

169
00:13:06,411 --> 00:13:11,082
MAJOR CRIMES UNIT 2

170
00:13:14,043 --> 00:13:15,086
You're back.

171
00:13:15,586 --> 00:13:17,547
Captain, we got the autopsy results.

172
00:13:18,756 --> 00:13:20,799
SUSPECT PROFILE
KIM GYEONGAE

173
00:13:27,348 --> 00:13:29,516
CARDIAC ARREST FROM
POTASSIUM CHLORIDE INJECTION

174
00:13:31,728 --> 00:13:34,229
Captain, I think you should see this.

175
00:13:34,230 --> 00:13:35,564
What is it?

176
00:13:35,565 --> 00:13:38,567
About the phone
that Ha Jeongsoo had on him…

177
00:13:38,568 --> 00:13:39,651
Yeah.

178
00:13:39,652 --> 00:13:41,904
It's the same number
that contacted Kim Gyeongae.

179
00:13:42,613 --> 00:13:44,198
- What?
- And here.

180
00:13:45,408 --> 00:13:48,369
They texted each other
on the date of Ms. Ko Seyun's abduction.

181
00:13:51,748 --> 00:13:53,040
SEONGJIN POLICE STATION

182
00:13:53,041 --> 00:13:56,294
Why were you looking for Mr. Ha?

183
00:13:57,086 --> 00:13:58,796
I had to ask him something.

184
00:13:59,380 --> 00:14:00,506
Ask him what?

185
00:14:01,674 --> 00:14:02,884
Kim Gyeongae…

186
00:14:05,053 --> 00:14:06,721
Why he tried to kill her.

187
00:14:07,221 --> 00:14:08,723
He tried to kill her?

188
00:14:09,807 --> 00:14:11,059
What do you mean by that?

189
00:14:12,310 --> 00:14:14,228
Two nights ago,

190
00:14:15,063 --> 00:14:19,232
I found him in her room and he had
a vial of potassium chloride in his hands.

191
00:14:19,233 --> 00:14:20,818
Potassium chloride?

192
00:14:21,319 --> 00:14:25,072
I barely stopped him from injecting it
into her IV without dilution.

193
00:14:33,539 --> 00:14:35,248
COME TO THE HOSPITAL
WE NEED TO TALK

194
00:14:35,249 --> 00:14:37,918
This message is from the phone
we found on Mr. Ha Jeongsoo.

195
00:14:37,919 --> 00:14:40,838
He sent it to Kim Gyeongae
on the day your wife was abducted.

196
00:14:42,131 --> 00:14:44,758
It seems he used this phone
only for contacting her.

197
00:14:44,759 --> 00:14:48,971
Mr. Ha was keeping her
updated on your movements, Mr. Kang.

198
00:14:52,016 --> 00:14:53,017
What's wrong?

199
00:14:57,355 --> 00:15:00,273
Dr. Ha told me that day at the hospital

200
00:15:00,274 --> 00:15:02,068
that he was only…

201
00:15:04,195 --> 00:15:06,822
doing as he was told.

202
00:15:06,823 --> 00:15:08,116
"Doing as he was told"?

203
00:15:08,741 --> 00:15:13,454
You mean someone else
put him up to kill Kim Gyeongae?

204
00:15:17,375 --> 00:15:19,418
That's what I'm not sure about.

205
00:15:20,545 --> 00:15:23,339
I went back
to the hospital to find that out.

206
00:15:30,138 --> 00:15:31,139
Ms. Kim.

207
00:15:32,557 --> 00:15:34,474
Ms. Kim? Can you hear me at all?

208
00:15:34,475 --> 00:15:35,559
Yeah.

209
00:15:40,523 --> 00:15:42,065
How's it going?

210
00:15:42,066 --> 00:15:44,151
- Hi.
- How's she looking?

211
00:15:44,152 --> 00:15:48,072
She's regained consciousness,
but she's still a bit out of it.

212
00:15:50,449 --> 00:15:51,450
Ms. Kim Gyeongae?

213
00:15:52,368 --> 00:15:53,369
We're with the police.

214
00:15:56,372 --> 00:16:00,333
This thing is a bit uncomfortable.

215
00:16:00,334 --> 00:16:02,253
You're currently under arrest.

216
00:16:02,837 --> 00:16:04,380
And your husband is a wanted man.

217
00:16:05,173 --> 00:16:08,050
Ms. Kim, why did you kidnap Ms. Ko Seyun?

218
00:16:12,263 --> 00:16:13,389
Ms. Kim.

219
00:16:14,599 --> 00:16:17,017
What was the purpose
of kidnapping Ko Seyun?

220
00:16:17,018 --> 00:16:20,271
Detective? The patient has
just regained consciousness.

221
00:16:20,938 --> 00:16:23,648
She needs rest
more than anything right now.

222
00:16:23,649 --> 00:16:25,568
Maybe you should continue another time.

223
00:16:32,491 --> 00:16:33,951
- Fair enough.
- Thank you.

224
00:16:35,411 --> 00:16:37,788
Both my husband and I…

225
00:16:40,124 --> 00:16:43,419
we were just pawns in this game.

226
00:16:47,632 --> 00:16:50,300
An update on
the major hospital kidnapping case.

227
00:16:50,301 --> 00:16:52,636
- Kidnapping?
- Police investigation has revealed

228
00:16:52,637 --> 00:16:55,180
that a doctor at the facility,
identified as Suspect B,

229
00:16:55,181 --> 00:16:57,974
ordered accomplice A
to kidnap the hospital chairwoman,

230
00:16:57,975 --> 00:16:59,809
- the director's daughter.
- My gosh.

231
00:16:59,810 --> 00:17:03,271
Suspect B was reportedly struggling
with multi-million-won private debt,

232
00:17:03,272 --> 00:17:06,816
and police now believe he took
his own life after the plot failed.

233
00:17:06,817 --> 00:17:08,860
Gosh, I feel so bad for Dr. Kang.

234
00:17:08,861 --> 00:17:11,447
The police were after him for days
when he was innocent.

235
00:17:12,240 --> 00:17:15,033
He looked like he had
wounds all over his body too.

236
00:17:15,034 --> 00:17:17,285
See? I told you.

237
00:17:17,286 --> 00:17:20,706
I said, Dr. Kang would never do
something like that, didn't I?

238
00:17:21,332 --> 00:17:23,166
But can you believe that about Dr. Ha?

239
00:17:23,167 --> 00:17:24,751
We used to see him every day here.

240
00:17:24,752 --> 00:17:27,963
He seemed so gentle.
But he was up to something so horrible?

241
00:17:27,964 --> 00:17:32,843
I mean, he made a lot of mistakes,
so I just thought he was a bit clumsy.

242
00:17:33,427 --> 00:17:35,263
Guess you can never really know someone.

243
00:17:35,846 --> 00:17:37,557
You're such a bad judge of character.

244
00:17:38,266 --> 00:17:40,392
I always knew he was trouble.

245
00:17:40,393 --> 00:17:41,936
That look in his eyes was…

246
00:17:42,645 --> 00:17:45,480
You know, he always seemed a bit on edge.

247
00:17:45,481 --> 00:17:47,148
Like he was nervous.

248
00:17:47,149 --> 00:17:50,110
The investigation into the high-profile
hospital kidnapping case,

249
00:17:50,111 --> 00:17:52,320
which shocked the public,
has taken a major turn.

250
00:17:52,321 --> 00:17:54,906
Suspect A, who has regained
consciousness after surgery,

251
00:17:54,907 --> 00:17:56,366
reportedly testified to police

252
00:17:56,367 --> 00:17:59,494
that they followed Suspect B's orders.

253
00:17:59,495 --> 00:18:01,496
Meanwhile, Dr. Kang,
who was once named a suspect…

254
00:18:03,207 --> 00:18:05,626
…has suffered from an overreaching
police investigation. Consequently--

255
00:18:11,924 --> 00:18:14,176
FRONT DOOR
SAVE, OPEN

256
00:18:25,479 --> 00:18:26,689
How are you feeling?

257
00:18:29,025 --> 00:18:30,233
Well, I'm fine,

258
00:18:30,234 --> 00:18:32,861
but what brings you out here?

259
00:18:32,862 --> 00:18:35,572
I wanted to apologize
for suspecting you.

260
00:18:35,573 --> 00:18:38,701
So I wanted to sit down
and have a cup of coffee with you.

261
00:18:39,910 --> 00:18:40,911
Yeah.

262
00:18:43,539 --> 00:18:45,291
You're not a very good liar.

263
00:18:47,835 --> 00:18:49,670
If you want to say something, say it.

264
00:18:53,633 --> 00:18:56,761
Once we find Noh Manhui, who's on the run,
this case will be closed.

265
00:18:59,597 --> 00:19:00,598
It's just that…

266
00:19:01,474 --> 00:19:02,558
it doesn't quite add up.

267
00:19:04,894 --> 00:19:07,146
Are you talking about Dr. Ha Jeongsoo?

268
00:19:10,983 --> 00:19:13,986
He said that he was only doing
as he was told.

269
00:19:14,987 --> 00:19:16,822
At first, I thought he was just lying

270
00:19:17,323 --> 00:19:18,991
to save his own skin.

271
00:19:20,117 --> 00:19:23,953
But the evidence fits together too neatly,
like someone set it all up.

272
00:19:23,954 --> 00:19:25,206
I can't put my finger on it,

273
00:19:25,998 --> 00:19:27,416
but it just doesn't feel right.

274
00:19:29,043 --> 00:19:31,379
It's as if I'm missing something.

275
00:19:33,714 --> 00:19:34,715
But then…

276
00:19:36,592 --> 00:19:38,636
your face tells me I'm not the only one.

277
00:19:42,264 --> 00:19:43,933
If you ever think of something,

278
00:19:44,934 --> 00:19:46,060
please let me know.

279
00:19:48,562 --> 00:19:49,563
Okay.

280
00:20:26,475 --> 00:20:28,518
If that's the case, I'd like to wait.

281
00:20:28,519 --> 00:20:29,729
Very well.

282
00:20:31,480 --> 00:20:33,899
Thank you, Dr. Ko. We're in your hands.

283
00:20:34,650 --> 00:20:35,651
Honey.

284
00:20:38,738 --> 00:20:40,990
Hmm.

285
00:20:59,675 --> 00:21:01,676
WOORI TOGETHER MEDICAL CENTER

286
00:21:03,888 --> 00:21:06,264
I believe the incident involving Dr. Ha

287
00:21:06,265 --> 00:21:09,017
has come
as a tremendous shock to all of us,

288
00:21:09,018 --> 00:21:13,230
including our medical staff
and everyone else involved.

289
00:21:14,940 --> 00:21:18,736
This case may have come to an end,

290
00:21:19,320 --> 00:21:21,739
but the patients remain uneasy.

291
00:21:22,448 --> 00:21:27,244
Our priority should be
getting the hospital back on track.

292
00:21:27,828 --> 00:21:29,079
Which is why…

293
00:21:31,749 --> 00:21:33,542
My apologies for being late.

294
00:21:40,382 --> 00:21:41,508
Sorry.

295
00:21:41,509 --> 00:21:43,052
Don't mind me.

296
00:21:46,514 --> 00:21:47,515
Uh…

297
00:21:48,098 --> 00:21:50,517
An arrest warrant has been issued
for Kim Gyeongae,

298
00:21:50,518 --> 00:21:52,895
who is currently our patient.

299
00:21:53,479 --> 00:21:56,649
As soon as she's stable,
she'll be transferred into police custody.

300
00:21:57,233 --> 00:21:59,067
In the meantime,

301
00:21:59,068 --> 00:22:03,155
I'd like Dr. Choi Chiung
to oversee her care.

302
00:22:03,906 --> 00:22:05,490
May I take over?

303
00:22:07,993 --> 00:22:08,994
Excuse me?

304
00:22:09,787 --> 00:22:10,996
I was asking

305
00:22:12,748 --> 00:22:15,125
if I could take point
on Kim Gyeongae's case, sir.

306
00:22:15,709 --> 00:22:17,127
Are you being serious right now?

307
00:22:18,045 --> 00:22:19,713
I operated on her.

308
00:22:20,756 --> 00:22:25,219
No one here knows her post-op course
and current condition better than I do.

309
00:22:26,720 --> 00:22:31,016
It makes more sense to keep me on her case
than pulling someone else in.

310
00:22:31,642 --> 00:22:35,395
With everything that's going on,
if you stay on this case,

311
00:22:35,396 --> 00:22:37,189
it'll only get people talking.

312
00:22:38,691 --> 00:22:39,983
Isn't it weirder to change

313
00:22:39,984 --> 00:22:42,486
attending physicians
just because people might talk?

314
00:22:44,238 --> 00:22:47,782
If there's anyone here who knows
about this patient better than I do,

315
00:22:47,783 --> 00:22:49,159
I'm happy to step aside.

316
00:22:56,000 --> 00:22:58,002
Otherwise, I'm staying on her case.

317
00:23:13,893 --> 00:23:15,102
How are you feeling?

318
00:23:17,146 --> 00:23:19,398
Wait, what's going on?

319
00:23:20,232 --> 00:23:21,524
What are you doing here?

320
00:23:21,525 --> 00:23:24,235
Acute bleeding developed around the tumor,

321
00:23:24,236 --> 00:23:26,155
so we had to perform an emergency surgery.

322
00:23:26,697 --> 00:23:30,241
The trauma caused the tumor to hemorrhage,
which compressed your nerves.

323
00:23:30,242 --> 00:23:33,119
We were able to drain the blood
and relieve that pressure.

324
00:23:33,120 --> 00:23:34,746
You should start improving now.

325
00:23:34,747 --> 00:23:37,832
Is that what you're here to talk about?

326
00:23:37,833 --> 00:23:40,376
Oh, I'll be your attending physician
starting today.

327
00:23:42,421 --> 00:23:43,756
What did you just say?

328
00:23:45,257 --> 00:23:46,884
Thanks to your testimony,

329
00:23:47,551 --> 00:23:49,135
my name was cleared,

330
00:23:49,136 --> 00:23:50,970
and I'm back at the hospital.

331
00:23:50,971 --> 00:23:53,390
It only feels right that I take your case.

332
00:23:54,183 --> 00:23:55,643
Just cut to the chase.

333
00:23:56,352 --> 00:23:57,978
What do you really want?

334
00:23:59,813 --> 00:24:02,566
You said Dr. Ha

335
00:24:03,275 --> 00:24:05,444
planned this whole thing by himself.

336
00:24:07,196 --> 00:24:08,781
But I just don't get it.

337
00:24:09,782 --> 00:24:11,992
The fact that you don't understand it

338
00:24:12,660 --> 00:24:14,620
doesn't make it any less true.

339
00:24:15,621 --> 00:24:19,917
I don't get why Dr. Ha did
what he did to me either.

340
00:24:26,757 --> 00:24:29,093
Remember what you said to me
before your surgery?

341
00:24:31,011 --> 00:24:32,221
You mean…

342
00:24:33,889 --> 00:24:37,851
"Extending other people's lifespans
by using those unborn babies."

343
00:24:38,978 --> 00:24:40,061
You mean that?

344
00:24:40,062 --> 00:24:41,438
About the fetal stem cells?

345
00:24:43,399 --> 00:24:44,691
How do you know about that?

346
00:24:44,692 --> 00:24:48,236
I signed up for the clinical trial
at this hospital.

347
00:24:48,237 --> 00:24:50,239
That's when I found out
what it was all about.

348
00:24:50,990 --> 00:24:52,366
But who cares, right?

349
00:24:52,866 --> 00:24:54,410
As long as I could get on the list.

350
00:24:55,285 --> 00:24:58,956
At first, I thought,
"How could he call himself a doctor?"

351
00:25:01,333 --> 00:25:03,961
But I was in no position to judge.

352
00:25:05,212 --> 00:25:06,463
What I didn't know

353
00:25:07,589 --> 00:25:11,677
was that he planned
to take advantage of us for his own good.

354
00:25:15,556 --> 00:25:18,642
That answers your question, doesn't it?

355
00:25:23,981 --> 00:25:25,273
This is unfair!

356
00:25:25,274 --> 00:25:27,568
I'm a victim in all of this too!

357
00:25:29,278 --> 00:25:31,196
If I had gotten that surgery,

358
00:25:31,947 --> 00:25:33,991
I wouldn't have taken things this far.

359
00:25:35,284 --> 00:25:36,285
But guess what?

360
00:25:38,370 --> 00:25:39,413
I didn't make the cut.

361
00:25:40,497 --> 00:25:43,792
My life was at stake,
but they made it sound so simple.

362
00:25:44,626 --> 00:25:47,629
There was no rhyme or reason to any of it.

363
00:25:50,466 --> 00:25:55,137
They dropped me from the surgery list
just because I'm an ex-con.

364
00:25:55,929 --> 00:26:00,100
They ruled you out
because of your criminal record?

365
00:26:01,769 --> 00:26:03,353
Who told you that?

366
00:26:04,772 --> 00:26:05,856
Was that Dr. Ha as well?

367
00:26:10,736 --> 00:26:12,905
Well, what does any of that matter now?

368
00:26:14,907 --> 00:26:16,450
It's all in the past.

369
00:26:17,367 --> 00:26:20,746
You should let it go, Doctor.

370
00:26:22,664 --> 00:26:23,665
All right.

371
00:26:24,792 --> 00:26:26,334
I'll see you on my next rounds.

372
00:26:26,335 --> 00:26:28,170
Take good care of yourself.

373
00:26:44,978 --> 00:26:47,856
There was no rhyme
or reason to any of it.

374
00:26:48,440 --> 00:26:53,027
They dropped me from the surgery list
just because I'm an ex-con.

375
00:27:00,369 --> 00:27:01,619
Hey, it's me.

376
00:27:01,620 --> 00:27:02,955
I have a favor to ask.

377
00:28:04,766 --> 00:28:05,934
Hey, Dr. Kang.

378
00:28:07,102 --> 00:28:08,185
What brings you here?

379
00:28:08,186 --> 00:28:10,856
I just had to take a look at something.

380
00:28:13,233 --> 00:28:14,234
I see.

381
00:28:15,027 --> 00:28:16,737
Right, see you around.

382
00:28:32,127 --> 00:28:33,587
Thanks. Appreciate it.

383
00:28:34,087 --> 00:28:35,964
What did you need the lab keycard for?

384
00:28:38,008 --> 00:28:39,635
I just had to look into something.

385
00:28:40,761 --> 00:28:41,845
What was it?

386
00:28:42,429 --> 00:28:47,559
It turns out, Kim Gyeongae signed up
for one of our clinical trials.

387
00:28:48,852 --> 00:28:50,811
- Clinical trial?
- Yeah.

388
00:28:50,812 --> 00:28:53,607
It might have something
to do with your getting kidnapped,

389
00:28:54,441 --> 00:28:58,194
so I wanted to look at some applications
and selection records,

390
00:28:58,195 --> 00:28:59,363
but they weren't there.

391
00:29:00,405 --> 00:29:01,865
I'm sure I've seen them there.

392
00:29:03,659 --> 00:29:05,160
Are you saying someone took them?

393
00:29:06,703 --> 00:29:10,707
Seyun, would you mind
looking into your father's study

394
00:29:11,500 --> 00:29:17,255
and seeing if you find any applications
or selection records in there?

395
00:29:21,051 --> 00:29:22,719
Is that what this was?

396
00:29:23,512 --> 00:29:26,848
Is that why you showed up
at my parents' house?

397
00:29:27,849 --> 00:29:29,267
Is this all…

398
00:29:32,145 --> 00:29:34,064
Is it related to my dad somehow?

399
00:29:37,067 --> 00:29:39,236
I can't tell you much right now.

400
00:29:41,321 --> 00:29:42,990
Why are you doing this to me again?

401
00:29:44,199 --> 00:29:45,574
You promised me.

402
00:29:45,575 --> 00:29:48,704
You said you'd explain everything
once we got out of there.

403
00:29:53,792 --> 00:29:55,167
I'm sorry.

404
00:29:55,168 --> 00:29:56,795
Is that all you can say?

405
00:29:59,172 --> 00:30:00,674
Forget it. Whatever.

406
00:30:11,059 --> 00:30:12,477
If I look in his study…

407
00:30:14,604 --> 00:30:16,523
and find whatever it is
you're looking for…

408
00:30:18,775 --> 00:30:20,652
you still won't
tell me anything, will you?

409
00:30:36,043 --> 00:30:37,044
Taeju.

410
00:30:38,837 --> 00:30:39,838
Hi, Myeonghui.

411
00:30:41,465 --> 00:30:43,258
Good to have you back.

412
00:30:43,842 --> 00:30:45,218
I was so worried.

413
00:30:47,387 --> 00:30:48,930
Thanks for the other night.

414
00:30:49,973 --> 00:30:51,058
Don't mention it.

415
00:30:52,142 --> 00:30:53,476
I trusted you.

416
00:30:53,477 --> 00:30:56,313
I knew you'd never do anything like that.

417
00:30:58,940 --> 00:31:00,025
Are you okay?

418
00:31:00,609 --> 00:31:02,194
You don't look so great.

419
00:31:02,986 --> 00:31:04,571
Yeah, I'm good.

420
00:31:21,379 --> 00:31:24,423
The rising number of
"lonely deaths" among elderly citizens

421
00:31:24,424 --> 00:31:28,177
living alone has become
a pressing social crisis.

422
00:31:28,178 --> 00:31:29,345
Welcome.

423
00:31:29,346 --> 00:31:31,931
…build a stronger safety net

424
00:31:31,932 --> 00:31:36,560
by implementing smart care services
powered by AI and IoT.

425
00:31:36,561 --> 00:31:38,062
Reporter Kim Jisu has the story.

426
00:31:38,063 --> 00:31:41,273
I'm here at a smart monitoring
center operated by the local government.

427
00:31:41,274 --> 00:31:43,859
Here, you can see
real-time data tracking and status…

428
00:31:43,860 --> 00:31:45,236
Get the one next to it.

429
00:31:45,237 --> 00:31:46,987
…of elderly residents living alone.

430
00:31:46,988 --> 00:31:51,534
If the motion sensors in their homes fail
to detect movement for a set period…

431
00:31:51,535 --> 00:31:53,786
- Yeah, that one works better.
-  This one?

432
00:31:53,787 --> 00:31:55,996
Yeah, the blade's way better.

433
00:31:55,997 --> 00:31:58,999
…the alarm goes off.
The government expects this initiative

434
00:31:59,000 --> 00:32:02,086
will allow local authorities
to respond to crises more rapidly

435
00:32:02,087 --> 00:32:05,256
and bridge the gaps
in our current social welfare system.

436
00:32:05,257 --> 00:32:07,550
This is Kim Jisu, reporting for NBS News.

437
00:32:07,551 --> 00:32:08,634
- Here.
- This just in.

438
00:32:08,635 --> 00:32:11,262
The criminal at the center
of national attention…

439
00:32:11,263 --> 00:32:12,763
Are you out to get somebody?

440
00:32:12,764 --> 00:32:14,723
- …of violent offenses…
- How'd you know?

441
00:32:14,724 --> 00:32:17,518
I've seen it all.

442
00:32:17,519 --> 00:32:19,688
It's only in their heads.

443
00:32:20,188 --> 00:32:21,773
Nobody actually has the guts for it.

444
00:32:22,524 --> 00:32:23,775
What about me?

445
00:32:24,526 --> 00:32:26,027
You look like a dreamer indeed.

446
00:32:27,946 --> 00:32:28,947
How much is it?

447
00:32:29,531 --> 00:32:30,906
It's 35,000 won.

448
00:32:30,907 --> 00:32:34,410
…fatally bludgeoning an acquaintance
over a financial dispute.

449
00:32:34,411 --> 00:32:37,121
Given her violent criminal history,
police are…

450
00:32:37,122 --> 00:32:39,707
She was bad news from the beginning.

451
00:32:39,708 --> 00:32:42,126
Why even bother treating trash like her?

452
00:32:42,127 --> 00:32:44,129
They should've just let her die.

453
00:32:44,754 --> 00:32:47,340
That piece of trash
doesn't deserve human rights.

454
00:32:48,800 --> 00:32:51,343
- I swear to God…
- Meanwhile, the third accomplice,

455
00:32:51,344 --> 00:32:54,430
Noh Manhui, remains at large.

456
00:32:54,431 --> 00:32:58,309
He is described as over 180 cm tall
with a heavy, muscular build.

457
00:32:58,310 --> 00:33:04,398
He was last seen wearing
a brown jacket and black pants.

458
00:33:04,399 --> 00:33:08,903
Police warn that Noh is known to be
highly impulsive and is likely armed.

459
00:33:08,904 --> 00:33:10,821
I look way better in person, don't I?

460
00:33:10,822 --> 00:33:12,323
…do not approach him

461
00:33:12,324 --> 00:33:15,327
and contact your local
law enforcement immediately.

462
00:33:16,453 --> 00:33:18,955
You think I'm just a dreamer?

463
00:33:22,626 --> 00:33:24,669
You have a terrible read on people.

464
00:33:47,859 --> 00:33:49,277
Yeah, come in.

465
00:33:54,950 --> 00:33:56,451
Dad, I brought you some tea.

466
00:34:00,497 --> 00:34:02,832
Thank you. Leave it right there.

467
00:34:06,127 --> 00:34:08,046
How are you feeling these days?

468
00:34:09,214 --> 00:34:10,548
Yeah, I'm fine.

469
00:34:11,466 --> 00:34:12,926
Take it easy, okay?

470
00:34:16,096 --> 00:34:19,015
With everything going on at the hospital,

471
00:34:20,016 --> 00:34:21,518
you must be pretty exhausted, huh?

472
00:34:22,018 --> 00:34:23,186
I'm fine.

473
00:34:27,941 --> 00:34:30,026
- I'll leave you alone now.
- All right.

474
00:34:30,944 --> 00:34:32,278
Well,

475
00:34:32,279 --> 00:34:34,406
has Taeju been giving you a hard time?

476
00:34:34,990 --> 00:34:36,073
Sorry?

477
00:34:36,074 --> 00:34:39,494
Don't let yourself get
dragged into his business.

478
00:35:55,445 --> 00:35:57,988
WOORI TOGETHER MEDICAL CENTER
CLINICAL TRIAL APPLICATION

479
00:36:05,205 --> 00:36:08,249
CLINICAL TRIAL APPLICATION
OH MINSEOK

480
00:36:11,002 --> 00:36:12,962
KIM GYEONGAE
NOH MANHUI

481
00:36:16,424 --> 00:36:18,051
So how much of a drop
are we talking?

482
00:36:18,968 --> 00:36:20,052
What?

483
00:36:20,053 --> 00:36:22,262
He was stable just this afternoon.

484
00:36:22,263 --> 00:36:24,015
Why are you telling me this now?

485
00:36:29,145 --> 00:36:31,147
Yeah, keep monitoring
Chairman Lee's vitals.

486
00:36:32,816 --> 00:36:34,693
What are you doing here?

487
00:36:35,318 --> 00:36:38,154
Oh, just picking up the tray from earlier.

488
00:36:40,407 --> 00:36:41,574
Don't stay up too late.

489
00:36:42,283 --> 00:36:43,284
Okay.

490
00:37:15,108 --> 00:37:16,276
Out of the way!

491
00:37:22,824 --> 00:37:29,497
SANJEONG HARDWARE
TOOLS, BOLTS NUTS, CONSTRUCTION MATERIALS

492
00:37:36,379 --> 00:37:37,505
Hello, sir.

493
00:37:43,178 --> 00:37:44,845
Captain.

494
00:37:44,846 --> 00:37:46,806
That thing's shattered.
It's beyond recovery.

495
00:37:47,682 --> 00:37:49,016
Do it the old-fashioned way.

496
00:37:49,017 --> 00:37:51,059
Canvas the area.

497
00:37:51,060 --> 00:37:52,644
- Yes, sir.
- Yeah.

498
00:37:52,645 --> 00:37:55,231
WOORI TOGETHER MEDICAL CENTER

499
00:37:59,110 --> 00:38:00,195
Ms. Ko.

500
00:38:01,696 --> 00:38:02,697
Dr. Cha.

501
00:38:06,659 --> 00:38:07,660
Are you okay?

502
00:38:08,661 --> 00:38:09,745
What do you mean?

503
00:38:09,746 --> 00:38:12,582
Oh, I heard about what happened.

504
00:38:13,750 --> 00:38:16,085
I can't imagine
how hard it must have been.

505
00:38:17,962 --> 00:38:19,047
I'm all right.

506
00:38:20,131 --> 00:38:23,343
It's amazing that you're already
back at work

507
00:38:24,135 --> 00:38:25,720
after such an ordeal.

508
00:38:28,640 --> 00:38:30,975
I don't think
I could've gotten through it.

509
00:38:34,813 --> 00:38:36,231
Even Taeju…

510
00:38:36,815 --> 00:38:38,608
Everyone seems to be struggling.

511
00:38:40,318 --> 00:38:41,319
"Taeju"?

512
00:38:44,572 --> 00:38:46,324
Have you been talking to my husband?

513
00:38:49,577 --> 00:38:53,248
If you need someone to talk to,

514
00:38:53,957 --> 00:38:55,667
my door is always open.

515
00:38:56,793 --> 00:38:58,627
Does he stop by your office often?

516
00:38:58,628 --> 00:39:00,046
I wouldn't say often.

517
00:39:00,672 --> 00:39:05,927
But sometimes, he stops by
to talk about what's on his mind.

518
00:39:07,554 --> 00:39:08,805
About what exactly?

519
00:39:12,141 --> 00:39:16,187
Oh, I guess he doesn't tell you
about our conversations.

520
00:39:16,813 --> 00:39:19,148
Naturally, I assumed
you knew all about it.

521
00:39:19,941 --> 00:39:21,609
Is there anything I should know about?

522
00:39:23,486 --> 00:39:24,737
No, it's just…

523
00:39:26,364 --> 00:39:29,033
I think he's trying to handle
too much on his own.

524
00:39:30,034 --> 00:39:32,160
Had I known he'd never talked
to you about it,

525
00:39:32,161 --> 00:39:33,996
I wouldn't have mentioned it.

526
00:39:33,997 --> 00:39:37,834
Counseling is confidential,
so I can't really share.

527
00:39:38,459 --> 00:39:41,880
I think you guys should
sit down and talk about it.

528
00:39:50,054 --> 00:39:51,222
I understand.

529
00:40:03,735 --> 00:40:06,237
DIRECTOR KANG TAEJU

530
00:40:09,616 --> 00:40:12,744
SCREENED OUT

531
00:40:17,415 --> 00:40:18,625
Come in.

532
00:40:21,002 --> 00:40:22,003
Hey, Seyun.

533
00:40:36,100 --> 00:40:37,393
What's this?

534
00:40:40,313 --> 00:40:41,689
It's what you were looking for.

535
00:40:42,732 --> 00:40:44,609
Documents regarding the clinical trial.

536
00:40:45,193 --> 00:40:47,195
Oh, thanks.

537
00:40:48,446 --> 00:40:51,991
And I'm sorry for getting you
involved in all this.

538
00:40:58,623 --> 00:41:00,583
I ran into somebody on my way here.

539
00:41:02,001 --> 00:41:03,169
Who?

540
00:41:08,675 --> 00:41:11,094
Someone you've been
talking to often lately.

541
00:41:17,433 --> 00:41:18,476
It was strange.

542
00:41:19,936 --> 00:41:21,938
To find out that someone else knows things

543
00:41:22,939 --> 00:41:24,565
that you've never talked to me about.

544
00:41:26,526 --> 00:41:28,111
- That's--
- It's fine.

545
00:41:29,529 --> 00:41:31,738
I wasn't looking for an explanation.

546
00:41:31,739 --> 00:41:32,740
It's just…

547
00:41:35,326 --> 00:41:37,120
I just can't help but think

548
00:41:37,870 --> 00:41:39,789
that there's so much
I don't know about you.

549
00:42:11,029 --> 00:42:12,112
What's up?

550
00:42:12,113 --> 00:42:15,908
Ms. Ko just came out
of Dr. Kang's office.

551
00:42:16,492 --> 00:42:19,620
But she didn't look too happy.

552
00:42:20,705 --> 00:42:23,166
I think there's something going on
between the two.

553
00:42:24,834 --> 00:42:25,917
Really?

554
00:42:25,918 --> 00:42:28,754
Look, I can't keep this up, okay?

555
00:42:28,755 --> 00:42:32,508
I did everything that you asked. Please.

556
00:42:33,092 --> 00:42:35,303
If someone ever finds out,

557
00:42:36,095 --> 00:42:37,138
I'll be in huge trouble.

558
00:42:37,722 --> 00:42:38,973
Wouldn't you rather

559
00:42:39,891 --> 00:42:42,642
see your grandma again
while she's still alive?

560
00:42:42,643 --> 00:42:43,644
What did you say?

561
00:42:44,228 --> 00:42:46,981
You didn't do anything to her, did you?

562
00:42:48,441 --> 00:42:50,818
What are you talking about?
I didn't do anything.

563
00:42:52,320 --> 00:42:53,404
Not yet anyway.

564
00:42:58,034 --> 00:42:59,869
I'm not asking for much.

565
00:43:00,495 --> 00:43:03,288
I just need you to be my eyes and ears

566
00:43:03,289 --> 00:43:05,666
and tell me how those two are doing.

567
00:43:06,292 --> 00:43:07,959
But until when?

568
00:43:07,960 --> 00:43:09,503
Today.

569
00:43:09,504 --> 00:43:10,713
It'll be over today.

570
00:43:11,839 --> 00:43:12,924
You got that?

571
00:43:14,175 --> 00:43:15,343
Yeah.

572
00:43:23,935 --> 00:43:26,062
WOORI TOGETHER MEDICAL CENTER

573
00:43:38,074 --> 00:43:39,658
KIM GYEONGAE

574
00:43:39,659 --> 00:43:41,410
SCREENED OUT

575
00:43:47,166 --> 00:43:48,583
CLINICAL TRIAL APPLICATION

576
00:43:48,584 --> 00:43:50,502
LEE SEONGUK

577
00:43:50,503 --> 00:43:51,504
ACCEPTED

578
00:43:55,258 --> 00:43:56,341
PARK DOHYEON

579
00:43:56,342 --> 00:43:57,843
ACCEPTED

580
00:43:57,844 --> 00:43:59,094
KIM HOJIN

581
00:43:59,095 --> 00:44:00,220
ACCEPTED

582
00:44:00,221 --> 00:44:02,347
OH MINSEOK
ACCEPTED

583
00:44:02,348 --> 00:44:03,640
SUNG JUIN

584
00:44:03,641 --> 00:44:05,810
ACCEPTED

585
00:44:19,782 --> 00:44:22,535
There was
no rhyme or reason to any of it.

586
00:44:23,035 --> 00:44:27,289
- Because I'm an ex-con.
- "Ex-convict."

587
00:44:27,290 --> 00:44:29,542
It doesn't say that anywhere.

588
00:44:53,482 --> 00:44:56,736
CALL LOG ANALYSIS REPORT
KIM GYEONGAE

589
00:45:01,782 --> 00:45:02,909
CHA MYEONGHUI

590
00:45:09,749 --> 00:45:12,752
MAIN BUILDING ELEVATOR #3

591
00:45:32,438 --> 00:45:35,441
DO NOT CROSS, UNDER INVESTIGATION
SANJEONG HARDWARE

592
00:45:36,651 --> 00:45:39,569
I looked when you guys called,
but I wasn't so sure about it.

593
00:45:39,570 --> 00:45:41,864
Okay, give us a sec. We'll look into it.

594
00:45:44,784 --> 00:45:46,284
This freaking bastard.

595
00:45:46,285 --> 00:45:47,619
Is it him?

596
00:45:47,620 --> 00:45:48,621
Yeah, it is.

597
00:45:49,705 --> 00:45:50,706
Wait, stop.

598
00:45:52,500 --> 00:45:53,668
What's the plate number?

599
00:46:39,338 --> 00:46:41,465
JEONGHAN GROUP
CEO LEE SEONGUK

600
00:46:42,425 --> 00:46:43,926
"Lee Seonguk."

601
00:46:44,552 --> 00:46:46,554
LEE SEONGUK

602
00:46:47,763 --> 00:46:49,515
"Park Dohyeon."

603
00:46:51,017 --> 00:46:52,434
"Kim Hojin. Sung Juin."

604
00:46:52,435 --> 00:46:53,853
ILO BIO
CEO PARK DOHYEON

605
00:46:54,729 --> 00:46:56,688
CEO KIM HOJIN

606
00:46:56,689 --> 00:46:57,772
CEO SUNG JUIN

607
00:46:57,773 --> 00:46:59,566
PARK DOHYEON
ACCEPTED

608
00:46:59,567 --> 00:47:01,776
KIM HOJIN

609
00:47:01,777 --> 00:47:03,528
SUNG JUIN

610
00:47:03,529 --> 00:47:05,281
OH MINSEOK

611
00:47:06,115 --> 00:47:08,033
OH MINSEOK

612
00:47:14,498 --> 00:47:16,542
It was all decided from the beginning.

613
00:47:17,418 --> 00:47:18,960
Those people had given up,

614
00:47:18,961 --> 00:47:22,131
but now, they're hopeful
and excited about the future.

615
00:47:23,341 --> 00:47:24,758
Couldn't you just

616
00:47:24,759 --> 00:47:28,804
let them have that hope?

617
00:47:37,855 --> 00:47:39,148
It wasn't about hope.

618
00:47:42,735 --> 00:47:44,779
It was all about money.

619
00:48:04,173 --> 00:48:07,176
BEHAVIORAL HEALTH
CONSULTATION ROOM

620
00:48:08,969 --> 00:48:11,472
Oh, gosh.
Sorry for dropping in on you like this.

621
00:48:12,556 --> 00:48:13,640
Not at all.

622
00:48:13,641 --> 00:48:17,186
But I've told you
everything I could about Dr. Ha.

623
00:48:17,686 --> 00:48:19,229
What more would you like to know?

624
00:48:19,230 --> 00:48:24,068
Well, we took another look
at the surveillance footage.

625
00:48:25,403 --> 00:48:26,529
Okay.

626
00:48:27,530 --> 00:48:29,407
From the elevator, the day he passed.

627
00:48:31,242 --> 00:48:35,162
You were on the elevator with him.

628
00:48:36,288 --> 00:48:40,792
And I noticed he pressed
the fourth floor at first.

629
00:48:42,253 --> 00:48:46,131
MAIN BUILDING E/V #3

630
00:48:46,132 --> 00:48:51,762
But then, he changed it
to the basement after you said something.

631
00:48:56,684 --> 00:48:57,685
Um…

632
00:48:58,352 --> 00:48:59,437
Did he really?

633
00:49:00,229 --> 00:49:01,479
I'm not sure.

634
00:49:01,480 --> 00:49:04,149
Yeah, that's what you said
the first time we talked.

635
00:49:04,150 --> 00:49:05,692
That you weren't sure.

636
00:49:05,693 --> 00:49:06,776
Yeah.

637
00:49:06,777 --> 00:49:11,407
And then you asked him if he was okay
because he didn't seem well, right?

638
00:49:12,616 --> 00:49:13,617
Yeah.

639
00:49:15,286 --> 00:49:16,912
But why would Mr. Ha

640
00:49:18,581 --> 00:49:20,749
switch floors after hearing that?

641
00:49:22,543 --> 00:49:23,835
Uh…

642
00:49:23,836 --> 00:49:25,212
That was before you got off.

643
00:49:27,089 --> 00:49:31,718
And after he switched floors,
you said something else to him.

644
00:49:42,563 --> 00:49:43,606
"Well done,"

645
00:49:44,899 --> 00:49:45,900
you said.

646
00:49:46,525 --> 00:49:47,526
Tell me.

647
00:49:48,569 --> 00:49:50,112
What did you mean by that?

648
00:49:56,994 --> 00:49:58,037
Ah.

649
00:49:59,079 --> 00:50:01,165
But the footage doesn't have any sound.

650
00:50:02,750 --> 00:50:06,629
How are you so sure about what I said?

651
00:50:10,966 --> 00:50:12,635
You know Kim Gyeongae, correct?

652
00:50:15,763 --> 00:50:17,681
I only talked to her during counseling.

653
00:50:19,225 --> 00:50:20,309
That's all.

654
00:50:21,060 --> 00:50:22,895
I think there's more to this story.

655
00:50:23,979 --> 00:50:28,692
You kept in touch with her
until just a month ago.

656
00:50:33,239 --> 00:50:37,159
CHA MYEONGHUI, HA JEONGSOO, NOH MANHUI,
SURVEY, CHA MYEONGHUI

657
00:50:39,286 --> 00:50:41,038
The day Mr. Ha died,

658
00:50:41,956 --> 00:50:43,290
you were in the same elevator.

659
00:50:44,959 --> 00:50:47,294
Plus, your recent contact
with Kim Gyeongae…

660
00:50:50,256 --> 00:50:51,507
Was this all a coincidence?

661
00:51:00,015 --> 00:51:02,017
We got the location
of Noh Manhui's vehicle.

662
00:51:02,518 --> 00:51:04,185
- He's on the move.
- Where is he?

663
00:51:04,186 --> 00:51:05,478
VEHICLE PLATE NUMBER TRACKING

664
00:51:05,479 --> 00:51:07,606
61K 9024
SILVER SUV

665
00:51:09,400 --> 00:51:11,235
Wait, we need to notify the captain.

666
00:51:14,738 --> 00:51:17,241
61K 9024

667
00:51:46,687 --> 00:51:47,938
It's you again.

668
00:51:48,856 --> 00:51:53,694
What do you have for me this time, Doctor?

669
00:51:55,863 --> 00:51:59,073
The real reason
you didn't make it onto the list.

670
00:52:02,328 --> 00:52:05,080
Okay. So, did you find anything?

671
00:52:11,670 --> 00:52:14,757
It's a list of the top sponsors
of this hospital. Have a look.

672
00:52:20,012 --> 00:52:24,266
The other one's the list of people
who made it into the trial.

673
00:52:25,434 --> 00:52:27,393
The exact same names.

674
00:52:27,394 --> 00:52:30,147
LEE SEONGUK, PARK DOHYEON, OH MINSEOK

675
00:52:34,151 --> 00:52:36,028
It was all about money.

676
00:52:36,987 --> 00:52:38,989
Your life depended on that surgery,

677
00:52:40,532 --> 00:52:43,619
but your fate was set in stone
from the very beginning.

678
00:52:44,870 --> 00:52:48,582
You didn't lose your spot.
You just never had one to begin with.

679
00:52:51,710 --> 00:52:52,711
But…

680
00:52:54,546 --> 00:52:58,717
Then why did they tell me
it was because I'm an ex-con?

681
00:53:07,935 --> 00:53:09,061
Who said that?

682
00:53:09,978 --> 00:53:13,857
I couldn't find any records of you
being an ex-con in the application,

683
00:53:15,234 --> 00:53:18,487
so who told you such a lie and why?

684
00:53:27,621 --> 00:53:29,873
Oh, if it wasn't Dr. Ha…

685
00:53:32,000 --> 00:53:33,168
Just my guess.

686
00:53:34,712 --> 00:53:37,756
If someone actually tried to
have you killed through Dr. Ha…

687
00:53:42,010 --> 00:53:44,805
That person is probably very happy
about this current situation.

688
00:53:48,225 --> 00:53:50,477
Do you think that person
will leave you alone now?

689
00:54:08,162 --> 00:54:09,288
Yeah, Detective Jang.

690
00:54:11,790 --> 00:54:12,791
What?

691
00:54:16,003 --> 00:54:18,005
Oh, yeah, I understand. Okay.

692
00:54:32,770 --> 00:54:35,646
INCOMING CALL
HUSBAND

693
00:55:27,449 --> 00:55:29,618
The doors are opening.

694
00:55:44,591 --> 00:55:45,717
CHAIRMAN'S OFFICE

695
00:56:00,190 --> 00:56:01,984
WOORI TOGETHER MEDICAL CENTER

696
00:56:58,915 --> 00:57:01,376
WING B, B3

697
00:57:09,843 --> 00:57:11,845
Did I leave it upstairs?

698
00:57:41,166 --> 00:57:43,042
INCOMING CALL
HUSBAND

699
00:58:04,147 --> 00:58:05,232
Ms. Ko.

700
00:58:07,150 --> 00:58:08,402
It's been a while.

701
00:58:13,365 --> 00:58:14,491
Where's Mr. Kang?

702
00:58:17,077 --> 00:58:18,578
MISSED CALL

703
00:58:33,301 --> 00:58:34,553
Don't move, okay?

704
00:58:40,016 --> 00:58:41,350
I said don't move!

705
00:58:41,351 --> 00:58:46,272
THE HUSBAND

706
00:59:27,397 --> 00:59:31,109
Who else knows about the hospital
using fetal stem cell samples?

707
00:59:31,943 --> 00:59:33,319
Ms. Cha Myeonghui has fled.

708
00:59:33,320 --> 00:59:35,864
-  Myeonghui?
-  She's a prime suspect.

709
00:59:36,448 --> 00:59:37,573
Was it Dr. Cha?

710
00:59:37,574 --> 00:59:40,535
The one who lied to you
that your prior got you rejected?

711
00:59:41,578 --> 00:59:43,120
Your husband should know as well.

712
00:59:43,121 --> 00:59:45,748
That you were both used and tossed aside.

713
00:59:45,749 --> 00:59:48,710
So now, you're all by yourself.

714
00:59:51,880 --> 00:59:54,131
Who ordered you to kidnap my wife?

715
00:59:54,132 --> 00:59:55,716
I wasn't after your wife.

716
00:59:55,717 --> 00:59:56,926
It was you.

717
00:59:56,927 --> 00:59:58,011
On whose orders and why?

718
00:59:58,720 --> 01:00:00,722
Translated by Hyun Sik Yoon
